# --- Works in languages the audience of this file does not read ------------
# Kept from the original script. These two are pruned by the language of the
# work, not by class, so they cut across every kind of publication.
.prune-nodes A P407 Q7850
.prune-nodes A P407 Q7737

# --- Editions, versions and other duplicates of a work ---------------------
.prune-nodes A P31 Q3331189

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT pruned, deliberately, and the first thing to revisit if the result is
# still too large. These are the everyday domains -- films, music, books,
# games -- and whether they belong in a "general purpose" local Wikidata is a
# judgement, not a fact. Uncomment a line to drop that domain; the counts are
# instances on 2026-03-09:
#
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q7725634    literary work                     408 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q11424      film                              324 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q482994     album                             304 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q105543609  musical work/composition          191 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q21191270   television series episode         176 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q7889       video game                        144 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q47461344   written work                      139 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q134556     single                            113 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q87167      manuscript                        104 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q125191     photograph                         77 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q5398426    television series                   79 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q27020041   sports season                      75 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q15416      television program                 60 k
#   .prune-nodes A P31 Q24862      short film                         48 k
#   .prune-facts A P161 B          cast member                      1.58 M facts
#   .prune-facts A P136 B          genre                            1.53 M facts
#   .prune-facts A P50 B           author                           1.21 M facts
#   .prune-facts A P407 B          language of work                 1.91 M facts
#
# Also left alone on purpose: P17 (country), which the original script tried
# to prune and never did. It answers a question people actually ask locally.
#
# Checked and deliberately NOT pruned, because their instances ARE
# classes -- they take part in P279 and pruning them would tear holes in
# the hierarchy this file exists to carry. The figures are how many of
# the class's instances took part in a P279 statement on 2026-03-09:
#
#   Q59199015   group of stereoisomers      148 451 of 148 476
#   Q2996394    biological process           28 323 of  42 508
#   Q417841     protein family               22 891 of  24 259
#   Q113813711  coin type                   14 652 of  65 129
#   Q67015883   group or class of enzymes    10 782 of  10 909
#   Q189118     cell type                     5 797 of   5 852
#   Q47154513   structural class of chem.     5 058 of   5 158
#   Q81505329   protein family w/ domain      4 532 of  12 958
#   Q898273     protein domain                2 898 of  11 735
#
# The rule they illustrate is worth applying to every candidate: a class
# whose name contains "family", "type", "class" or "group" almost always
# collects CLASSES, not individuals. Before adding a line, count
# `(zelph/targets n P279)` and `(zelph/sources P279 n)` over its
# instances; if that is not near zero, leave it out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.cleanup
